# Client structure

Work in **`client/`**, not `frontend/`. Call the API through `src/lib/api.ts`. Pass paths like `/auth/me`, not `/api/auth/me`. Client env is **`client/.env` only** (`VITE_API_URL` empty in local dev, API origin in production).

## Pages are folders

Each route lives under `client/src/pages/<page-name>/`:

```text
pages/
  login/
    LoginPage.tsx
    components/     # only used by this page
    hooks/          # only used by this page
  register/
    RegisterPage.tsx
    components/
    hooks/
  home/
    HomePage.tsx
    components/
```

- Keep `*Page.tsx` thin: compose page components + hooks.
- Page-only UI → `pages/<page>/components/`.
- Page-only hooks → `pages/<page>/hooks/`.
- Do **not** dump page-specific files into global `components/` or `hooks/`.

## Shared `components/` — sorted by role

```text
components/
  ui/         # Button, Input, Select, Modal, Table, …
  feedback/   # LoadingState, EmptyState, ErrorBanner, …
  layout/     # AppLayout, Sidebar, PageHeader, …
  forms/      # shared form helpers used by multiple pages
```

- Put a shared piece here only after it is reused ~2–3 times (or clearly cross-page).
- Prefer importing from the category folder (e.g. `components/ui/Button`).

## Shared hooks

- Cross-page hooks only (e.g. `useAuth`) live in `src/hooks/`.
- Everything else stays under the page folder.

## App shell (SPA — no full page reloads)

- **`main.tsx`** — mount the app and wrap it with **all** global providers. Do not put providers in `App.tsx`, layouts, or pages. Current stack (outer → inner): `QueryClientProvider` → `BrowserRouter` → `AuthProvider` → `ThemeProvider` → `App`. Keep `ThemeProvider` inside `AuthProvider` so it can read the session. Providers stay mounted so session and theme survive route changes.
- **`App.tsx`** — route table only (`Routes` / `Route`). No providers here.
- Navigate with **`Link`** or **`useNavigate`** from `react-router-dom` — never plain `<a href="/…">` for in-app links (that triggers a full reload).

## Server state (TanStack Query)

- **Library:** `@tanstack/react-query` for all API reads/writes from page hooks and shared auth.
- **`src/lib/queryClient.ts`** — shared `queryClient` instance and `toQueryErrorMessage()` (maps `ApiError` to user-facing strings).
- **Page hooks** — use `useQuery` for reads and `useMutation` for writes. Export a `*QueryKeys` object per domain (e.g. `expenseQueryKeys`) for cache keys and invalidation.
- **Auth** — `useAuth` loads `/auth/me` via `useQuery`; login/register call `setQueryData`, logout clears the cache, `refresh()` invalidates.
- **Defaults** (`queryClient.ts`): `retry: 1`, `refetchOnWindowFocus: false`. Override per hook when needed (e.g. auth `retry: false`).
- Do **not** fetch API data with raw `useEffect` + `useState` — use React Query.

## Theme preference

- **`src/lib/theme.ts`** — `ThemePreference`, `applyThemePreference()`, and localStorage helpers (`readStoredThemePreference`, `persistThemePreference`).
- **`ThemeProvider`** (`src/hooks/useTheme.tsx`) — local-first during the session: toggle updates localStorage and the DOM immediately; `PATCH /auth/me/theme` runs in the background. Rapid toggles are allowed; if a stale API response does not match the current local value, ignore it (local wins).
- **Page refresh / first session load** — when auth resolves for a user, apply the server `themePreference` once and refresh localStorage (API wins). Do not re-apply from auth cache updates during the same session.
